ize:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;"><a href=3D"#upcoming"=
 style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Upcoming Earnings</a></li=
></ul></td></tr></table><h2 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', =
serif;font-size:21px;color:#12395b;margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:4px;bord=
er-bottom:2px solid #12395b;"><a name=3D"news" id=3D"news"></a>Healthcare Dig=
est - In the News</h2><h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', se=
rif;font-size:17px;color:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;">Executive Summary</h3>
<ul style=3D"margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:22px;">
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">CMS offered states a hold-harmless per=
iod through June 30, 2027, delaying Medicaid work-requirement coverage losses=
 while preserving eligibility assessments and systems implementation. (<a hre=
f=3D"https://www.medicaid.gov/Federal-Policy-Guidance/Downloads/smd26006.pdf"=
 style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>Optional Hold Ha=
rmless Period for Community Engagement Implementation</em>, November 13, 2026=
</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">HealthSpan raised its Surgery Partners=
 offer to $25 per share and accepted stronger closing obligations after a com=
peting proposal, increasing both the value and closing probability of the nat=
ional ambulatory-surgery platform. (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/e=
dgar/data/1638833/000110465926124243/tm2629312d1_8k.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e=
9a;text-decoration:underline;">SEC, <em>Surgery Partners Form 8-K</em>, Novem=
ber 9, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">CMS extended the nationwide hospice an=
d home-health enrollment moratoria for six months but allowed enrolled operat=
ors to add locations, shifting the policy=E2=80=99s competitive advantage tow=
ard incumbent expansion.</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Federal prior-authorization policy mov=
ed from technical specifications to production-like workflow testing, creatin=
g near-term integration work for payers, EHRs and intermediaries without prov=
iding a compliance safe harbor. (<a href=3D"https://healthit.gov/news/onc-and=
-cms-launch-industry-electronic-prior-authorization-testing-initiative/" styl=
e=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">ONC, <em>ONC and CMS Launch In=
dustry Electronic Prior Authorization Testing Initiative</em>, November 12, 2=
026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Overall environment: modestly improved=
 for payers, providers and health technology because Medicaid coverage disrup=
tion was deferred and implementation demand increased, although entry restric=
tions and P3=E2=80=99s financing exposure show continued pressure on smaller =
operators.</li>
</ul>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-1" name=3D"story-1" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>1. CMS turns first-half 2027 Medi=
caid work checks into a shadow eligibility period</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">States may suspend Medicaid eligibilit=
y denials and disenrollments tied solely to community-engagement noncomplianc=
e through June 30, 2027. They must still assess qualifying activities, deemed=
 compliance and exclusions for relevant applications and renewals beginning J=
anuary 1. CMS will exclude cases handled under an approved mitigation plan fr=
om PERM, Medicaid Eligibility Quality Control and other beneficiary-eligibili=
ty audit errors. States seeking the option from January 1 should notify CMS b=
y December 11. (<a href=3D"https://www.medicaid.gov/Federal-Policy-Guidance/D=
ownloads/smd26006.pdf" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS=
, <em>Optional Hold Harmless Period for Community Engagement Implementation</=
em>, November 13, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The policy defers the first wave of wo=
rk-related coverage losses, supporting Medicaid MCO membership and reducing n=
ear-term uncompensated-care exposure for providers. It does not reduce implem=
entation scope. States still need data matching, exclusion logic, notices, ca=
seworker workflows and auditable eligibility decisions.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">January through June becomes a product=
ion testing period in states adopting the option. Eligibility vendors gain ad=
ditional time to correct system defects, while MCOs and providers retain more=
 opportunity to intervene before adverse determinations. Variation will remai=
n high because states can decline the option or use it for a shorter period.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">State mitigation-plan decisions by Dec=
ember 11 and whether CMS litigation or additional guidance changes the July 1=
 enforcement threshold.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-2" name=3D"story-2" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>2. A rival bid raises the price a=
nd closing obligations for Surgery Partners</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">HealthSpan Partners increased its offe=
r for Surgery Partners to $25 per share, lifting enterprise value from approx=
imately $5.7 billion to as much as $6.0 billion after Surgery Partners receiv=
ed an unsolicited competing proposal. The amendment adds a 10% annualized tic=
king fee after March 1, 2027, capped at $1.61 per share, and removes the mate=
riality limit from HealthSpan=E2=80=99s obligation to take actions needed to =
resolve antitrust impediments. The termination fee increased to approximately=
 $149.1 million. (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1638833/=
000110465926124243/tm2629312d1_8k.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration=
:underline;">SEC, <em>Surgery Partners Form 8-K</em>, November 9, 2026</a>)</=
p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Surgery Partners also reported 6.0% sa=
me-facility revenue growth, driven by 5.8% higher revenue per case and only 0=
.2% case growth. (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1638833/=
000163883326000089/exhibit991q32026earningsre.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;tex=
t-decoration:underline;">SEC, <em>Surgery Partners Third Quarter 2026 Results=
</em>, November 9, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The amendment strengthens last week=E2=
=80=99s thesis that scaled ASC networks have become scarce strategic assets f=
or health systems. Competing interest raised the purchase price despite limit=
ed underlying volume growth, indicating that geographic reach, physician rela=
tionships and site-of-care positioning carry substantial option value.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The expanded regulatory covenant impro=
ves closing certainty but may require HealthSpan to accept divestitures or op=
erating restrictions. Payers should assess concentration and reimbursement ex=
posure in markets where Surgery Partners overlaps with Bon Secours Mercy Heal=
th.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The identity of the rival bidder, the =
proxy filing and any antitrust remedy affecting local ASC ownership or contra=
cting.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-3" name=3D"story-3" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>3. CMS extends the home-health an=
d hospice entry freeze while letting incumbents add locations</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS extended nationwide moratoria on i=
nitial Medicare enrollment of home-health agencies and hospices, including ce=
rtain changes in majority ownership, for another six months. Unlike the May m=
oratoria, currently enrolled organizations may now add practice locations. CM=
S said an October California operation produced 145 revocations involving pro=
viders associated with more than $703 million in Medicare and Medicaid paymen=
ts. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/cms-extends-modif=
ies-nationwide-freeze-new-medicare-hospice-home-health-enrollment-six-months-=
combat" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>CMS Exten=
ds and Modifies Nationwide Freeze on New Medicare Hospice and Home Health Enr=
ollment</em>, November 12, 2026</a>; <a href=3D"https://public-inspection.fed=
eralregister.gov/2026-23242.pdf" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:under=
line;">Federal Register, <em>Extension and Modification of the Nationwide Tem=
porary Moratorium on Enrollment of Hospices</em>, November 16, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The extension adds a market-structure =
effect to last week=E2=80=99s retroactive-revocation policy. Greenfield Medic=
are entry and some control transactions remain blocked, while established ope=
rators can expand through additional locations. Scaled incumbents therefore g=
ain a six-month advantage in recruiting clinicians, entering adjacent service=
 areas and negotiating payer relationships.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The ownership restriction may also com=
plicate acquisitions structured around new billing enrollments or majority-co=
ntrol changes. Diligence must address enrollment continuity, managing personn=
el and whether a transaction falls within the moratorium rather than treating=
 provider numbers as routine closing items.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Access indicators in rural markets, fu=
rther payment suspensions and whether CMS extends or narrows the moratoria ag=
ain in May 2027.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-4" name=3D"story-4" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>4. Federal prior-authorization te=
sting shifts the risk from APIs to end-to-end workflow</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">ONC and CMS launched voluntary 10- to =
12-week testing sprints for payers, providers, EHR developers and intermediar=
ies using production-like environments. Testing will cover the Da Vinci Cover=
age Requirements Discovery, Documentation Templates and Rules, and Prior Auth=
orization Support implementation guides. MITRE will support recruitment and c=
oordination, while Drummond Group will operate the FHIRplace testing environm=
ent. Organizations must express interest by November 20; participation does n=
ot constitute certification or a CMS compliance determination. (<a href=3D"ht=
tps://healthit.gov/news/onc-and-cms-launch-industry-electronic-prior-authoriz=
ation-testing-initiative/" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"=
>ONC, <em>ONC and CMS Launch Industry Electronic Prior Authorization Testing =
Initiative</em>, November 12, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The initiative recognizes that standar=
ds conformance does not ensure an operational authorization. The remaining fa=
ilure points sit between organizations: coverage-rule discovery, clinical-doc=
ument generation, identity matching, attachments, exception handling and stat=
us reconciliation.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">That increases demand for workflow orc=
hestration, test data, monitoring and implementation services around payer an=
d EHR APIs. Clearinghouses and interoperability vendors can capture work that=
 neither payer cores nor EHRs manage alone. Voluntary testing may reduce depl=
oyment risk, but organizations remain responsible for compliance and cannot t=
reat participation as a safe harbor.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The first-round participants, selected=
 clinical use cases and whether sprint findings become formal implementation =
guidance or change enforcement expectations.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-5" name=3D"story-5" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>5. P3=E2=80=99s margin recovery s=
till leaves a financing problem</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">P3 Health reported third-quarter adjus=
ted EBITDA of $20.9 million versus a $45.9 million loss a year earlier. Medic=
al margin reached $43.9 million, or $140 per member per month, but fell to $3=
5.0 million and $111 PMPM after excluding payer settlements and prior-year de=
velopment. At-risk membership declined 9% to approximately 105,000 following =
network and payer rationalization. (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/e=
dgar/data/1832511/000183251126000045/piii-20261109xexx991.htm" style=3D"color=
:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">SEC, <em>P3 Health Partners Third Quarte=
r 2026 Results</em>, November 9, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">P3 nevertheless reported $43.9 million=
 of unrestricted cash, a $190.6 million working-capital deficit and $90.1 mil=
lion of nine-month operating cash use, concluding that substantial doubt rema=
ins about its ability to continue as a going concern. (<a href=3D"https://www=
.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1832511/000183251126000046/piii-20260930.htm" st=
yle=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">SEC, <em>P3 Health Partners =
Form 10-Q</em>, November 9, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The result strengthens the case that s=
elective payer and provider contraction can repair value-based-care unit econ=
omics. It weakens the assumption that positive adjusted EBITDA resolves the s=
ector=E2=80=99s capital problem. Settlement timing, preferred obligations, de=
bt maturities and claims funding can still overwhelm reported operating impro=
vement.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Health-plan and physician partners sho=
uld treat liquidity as a service-continuity and counterparty risk. Smaller en=
ablement platforms may need refinancing, asset sales or strategic capital bef=
ore their improved medical margins convert into sustainable cash generation.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">P3=E2=80=99s capital-raising or refina=
ncing plan and recurring 2027 medical margin after prior-period benefits fall=
 away.</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;">What to Watch For</h3>
<ul style=3D"margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:22px;">
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">November 20, 2026: Organizations must =
express interest in the first ONC-CMS electronic prior-authorization testing =
round. (<a href=3D"https://healthit.gov/news/onc-and-cms-launch-industry-elec=
tronic-prior-authorization-testing-initiative/" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-d=
ecoration:underline;">ONC, <em>ONC and CMS Launch Industry Electronic Prior A=
uthorization Testing Initiative</em>, November 12, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">December 7, 2026: Medicare annual enro=
llment ends, providing the first firm membership read after 2027 benefit and =
Stars changes. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/medica=
re-advantage-medicare-prescription-drug-programs-expected-remain-stable-2027"=
 style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>Medicare Advanta=
ge and Medicare Prescription Drug Programs Expected to Remain Stable in 2027<=
/em>, October 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">December 11, 2026: States intending to=
 use the Medicaid work-requirement hold-harmless option from January 1 are as=
ked to notify CMS. (<a href=3D"https://www.medicaid.gov/Federal-Policy-Guidan=
ce/Downloads/smd26006.pdf" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"=
>CMS, <em>Optional Hold Harmless Period for Community Engagement Implementati=
on</em>, November 13, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">December 15, 2026: Comments close on C=
MS=E2=80=99s proposed MA provider-directory and Part D PBM accountability rul=
e. (<a href=3D"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-21420.pdf" =
style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Federal Register, <em>CMS-=
4214-P</em>, October 20, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;">Bottom Line</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS=E2=80=99s Medicaid hold-harmless o=
ption is the week=E2=80=99s most important economic change because it defers =
first-half 2027 coverage losses while preserving the full eligibility-technol=
ogy build. State implementation choices and resulting MCO membership variatio=
n need the closest attention. The December 11 notification date is the next e=
vent most likely to determine how much coverage and provider-cash exposure mo=
ves from January into the second half of 2027.</p><h2 style=3D"font-family:Ge=
orgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:21px;color:#12395b;margin:28px 0 10=
px;padding-bottom:4px;border-bottom:2px solid #12395b;"><a name=3D"earnings" =
id=3D"earnings"></a>Recent Earnings Highlights</h2><h3 style=3D"font-family:G=
eorgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;color:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8=
px;"><a name=3D"earnings-hims" id=3D"earnings-hims"></a>Hims &amp; Hers (<a h=
